7. Lambda example — AWS Service trust

Another useful AWS Service example.

{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "LambdaTrust",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {
        "Service": "lambda.amazonaws.com"
      },
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
    }
  ]
}

Permissions:

{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "CloudWatchLogs",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "logs:CreateLogGroup",
        "logs:CreateLogStream",
        "logs:PutLogEvents"
      ],
      "Resource": "*"
    }
  ]
}

Flow:

Lambda
  ↓
Lambda Execution Role
  ↓
CloudWatch Logs
8. ECS Task Role — another important AWS Service example

For ECS, don't confuse the task role and execution role.

Task role trust:

{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {
        "Service": "ecs-tasks.amazonaws.com"
      },
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
    }
  ]
}

Permissions could be:

{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "s3:GetObject"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::my-app-bucket/*"
    }
  ]
}

Flow:

ECS Task
  ↓
Task Role
  ↓
S3